the view from a security camera of what  has now been declared a terrorist  incident just before 11 o'clock on  remembrance sunday morning a bomb went  off in a taxi outside liverpool women's  hospital injuring the driver and killing  the male passenger as the taxi  approached the drop-off point at the  hospital an explosion occurred from  within the car this quickly engulfed it  in flames  remarkably the taxi driver escaped from  the cab  he's been treated for his injuries that  he sustained and he's now been released  from hospital as the emergency services  descended on the hospital a major  incident was declared and anti-terror  police moved quickly  the taxi's passenger had been picked up  in rutland avenue in sefton park a mile  away from the explosion armed officers  sealed off the street and say they found  significant items there eight families  have been evacuated from their homes  this afternoon at sefton park a  controlled explosion was heard while  sky's fraser moore was reporting from  the scene  and detonated or ignited they said  by the passenger just heard a loud bang  from the other side of where i'm  standing here not sure what that was  merseyside police later confirmed the  explosion was part of their operation  and said there was no risk to the public  on sunday further north in the  kensington area of the city more streets  were sealed off and four men aged 20 to  29 were arrested under the terrorism act  three on sunday and one on monday  morning  the taxi driver has now been named as  david perry his wife rachel posted  online he is without doubt lucky to be  alive the explosion happened whilst he  was in the car and how he managed to  escape is an utter miracle he certainly  had some guardian angels looking over  him  the police think mr perry's passenger  had built the bomb himself but they  don't know why he went to the women's  hospital or why it detonated when it did  we are of course aware that there are  remembrance events just a short distance  away from the hospital and that the  ignition occurred shortly before 11am  we cannot at this time draw any  connection with this but it is a line of  inquiry which we are pursuing this  investigation is said to be moving at  pace detectives have much to go on mr  perry as an eyewitness and what they  believe to be a crime scene here in  rutland avenue as a result of this  explosion the uk's terror threat level  has been raised from substantial to  severe meaning an attack is now judged  to be highly likely  the police say their work here on the  ground could last for several days  gerard tub sky news liverpool
 

